## Summary

I shipped a production-polished, Apple-idiomatic **`ShareDriveDialog`** at parity with `web/src/features/driving/components/ShareDriveDialog.tsx`, following the established modals-dialogs architecture (state-holder + seams + projection core + SwiftUI view layer).

**Delivered** (12 files, committed `f18216e2f`): `ShareDriveDialog.{Adapter,Seams,Model,swift,States,Views,Controls,Rows,Previews,strings,Tests,ModelTests}` — every file ≤ 376 lines.

**Parity reproduced**: the always-present create form (title `Input`, include-speed/telemetry `Toggle`s, expiry `Select`, "Generate Link"), the success result panel (`${origin}/s/{token}` URL + Copy + open + "Create another link"), and the existing-links list (title/Untitled, views, Expired/Expires{date}/No expiry, copy + revoke). Data binds via P1/S8 seams (`useShareLinks`/`useCreateShareLink`/`useRevokeShareLink`) — no HTTP in the view. Every state renders: loading / empty / error+retry / content, plus create-pending, per-row revoke spinner, inline errors, and stale/offline freshness.

